  "limitations": [
    "Current candidate evaluation is failed because FoundationDB does not provide production-grade user-level access-control isolation for this scope; upstream documentation states connected clients can read and write every key, while tenants remain experimental and are not accepted as a production boundary.",
    "Provider capability evidence supports durability, atomic transactions, strict multi-writer serializability, distributed multi-host architecture, and backup/restore as candidate capabilities; deployment-dependent restart, conflict/failure behavior, migration/rollback, privacy-safe observability, and operational ownership remain pending.",
    "Current GoreeCloud production topology has one VPS and cannot qualify the intended failure-isolated multi-host deployment; at least three genuinely failure-isolated hosts plus exact network, TLS, backup, restore, observability, and rollback qualification would still be required for any revised candidate.",
    "This failed candidate evaluation is non-authorizing and does not select a provider, authorize infrastructure purchase or deployment, create production acceptance, or establish Privacy Shield production readiness."
  ]
